# Patterns match the whole context path, so a bare name only matches at the top
# level. Anything that can appear in a subdirectory is written as **/<name>.

# Never let a local secret into an image layer. `.env*` covers .env.local and
# .env.development.local, both of which name a private engine address.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Installed fresh by `npm ci` in the deps stage. Copying the host's tree in
# would be slow, and on a different platform it would be wrong: native modules
# are built for the machine that installed them.
**/node_modules

# Build output. A stale .next from the host would be copied over the top of the
# one this build produces, which is how an image ships last week's bundle.
.next
out
build
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test and lint detritus. The image does not run any of it.
coverage
bench
**/.DS_Store

# Local dev harness data written by scripts/dev-seed.mjs.
.dev

# Never read from inside the image. Excluded by extension rather than by name
# so adding a document does not bust the npm install layer.
.git
.github
.githooks
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
**/*.md
